  "problem": "If $X={m,n}$, then $P(X)=$",
  "worked_solution": "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $\u2205.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14095809/assets/f2f49123932a9877518a879e95410a4db3c4534f6d7709dbe56623037987cc0f.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n\u2205={},\\,{m},\\,{n},\\,{m,n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)={\u2205,{m},{n},{m,n}}.\n$$",
